The web UI moves from MUI to **Graphite**, a design system for dense, data-heavy desktop apps with a dark and a light theme from one token set ([ADR 0019](docs/adr/0019-graphite-design-system.md)). MUI, its icons and Emotion are removed.

Stacked on #20 (`ftr/finishing`); GitHub retargets this to `develop` once #20 is merged and its branch deleted.

## What changes

- **Graphite, vendored.** The React library lives in `frontend/graphite/` and is imported as `@graphite/react` through an alias, without a build step. Four small local changes are listed in its README so they can be re-applied on updates:
  - React 19 ref types;
  - no Google Fonts import;
  - Select announced as a combobox;
  - translatable labels.
- **What Graphite lacks, in `src/ui/`.** Built on its tokens and `g-` classes:
  - dialog (focus handling, rest of the page hidden from assistive technology);
  - alert, tooltip, chips and chip links;
  - select and multi-select;
  - comboboxes: pick one, free text with suggestions, several values as chips;
  - buttons and links with icons, table, progress, disclosure, text area.

  Lists and tooltips render into `<body>`, so tables and dialogs don't clip them. Covered by `src/ui/ui.test.tsx`.
- **Icons and fonts.** Icons are Lucide at Graphite's 16px / 1.5px stroke. Geist and Geist Mono are bundled from `@fontsource`, so the UI makes no third-party requests; fonts stay files, not inlined CSS.
- **Shell.** On wide screens the side menu collapses to a rail of icons; on narrow screens it slides in over the page. The color mode (system / light / dark) is kept in `localStorage` and applied by `index.html` before the app loads.
- **Charts and editor.** Charts stay ECharts with colors from Graphite's chart tokens (ADR 0015). The DSL editor stays CodeMirror, themed with Graphite's CSS variables (ADR 0016).
- **Pages.** Every page is restyled with Graphite type classes plus a plain CSS file per area (`tr-<area>-` classes). Roles and accessible names are unchanged.
- **Docs.** CLAUDE.md, the frontend README, both changelogs and the superseded parts of ADRs 0011, 0015 and 0016 are updated.

## Tests

Tests query by role and name, so they barely changed. The few that did:
- the menu rail;
- checkable color-mode items (`menuitemcheckbox`);
- named remove buttons on tags and chips;
- the tag field being a plain text box rather than a combobox;
- an `axis` color in the chart color fixture.

## Checks

- `frontend/test.sh` passes: lint, type check, 224 tests, build.
- Checked in a browser against the local stack in light and dark mode and at phone width: run list and filters, run detail, a dialog, the case execution charts.
- The derived metrics pages were also checked in a browser during the migration.

